{"game": "palworld", "language": "english", "appid": 1623730, "month": "2024-03", "window": 1, "start_date": 1709251200, "end_date": 1709855999, "month_true_total": 5958, "quota": 10, "returned": 10, "pulled_at": "2026-10-07 16:56:50 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "160069861", "author": {"steamid": "76561199646028398", "personaname": "idrees", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199646028398/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 4, "playtime_forever": 50147, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 127, "playtime_at_review": 6636, "last_played": 1791320154, "avatar": "fef49e7fa7e1997310d705b2a6158ff8dc1cdfeb"}, "language": "english", "review": "I really enjoy open world games. I believe saying it is Pokemon with guns, does the game a disservice. Even though they are Pokemon like creatures, that is where the similarities stop. Its a open world even to where you can build it as you see fit. You can play the whole time advance and grow and never challenge not a single boss. Do whatever your mood strikes you to do. I my favorite part is the ability to climb almost anything. No Pokemon game allows you to craft and build, enables you to die from environmental changes, or have zero story line to follow. Even though Palworld has obvious improvements make to a early access game there's still a lot of fun to be had in the game in itself. Most folks who have stepped away from it have played it on easy and blown through the game. I'm currently level 40-41 with 110 hrs of game play at normal difficulty. there are still bosses and dungeons I haven't encountered yet. Sorry for rambling but its a great game and will get better as they work towards completing it.", "timestamp_created": 1709855943, "timestamp_updated": 1709855943, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "pri